{number: 93}
{title: He Leadeth Me! O Blessed Tho’t}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] He leadeth me! O [F] blessed thought!
O [C] words with heav'nly [G7] comfort fraught!
What-[C] e'er I do, wher-[F] e'er I be,
Still [C] 'tis God's hand that [G7] leadeth [C] me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
He [C] leadeth me, He [F] leadeth me,
By [C] His own hand He [G7] leadeth me:
His [C] faithful foll'wer [F] I would be,
For [C] by His hand He [G7] leadeth [C] me.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
Some-[C] times 'mid scenes of [F] deepest gloom,
Some-[C] times where Eden's [G7] bowers bloom,
By [C] waters still, o'er [F] troubled sea,
Still [C] 'tis His hand that [G7] leadeth [C] me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
Lord, [C] I would clasp Thy [F] hand in mine,
Nor [C] ever murmur [G7] nor repine;
Con-[C] tent, whatever [F] lot I see,
Since [C] 'tis my God that [G7] leadeth [C] me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
And [C] when my task on [F] earth is done,
When, [C] by Thy grace, the [G7] vict'ry's won,
E'en [C] death's cold wave I [F] will not flee,
Since [C] God through Jordan [G7] leadeth [C] me.
{end_of_verse}
